  **§3 裁决：**
  - U1 纳入 R1: reasonable. Risk: 修改断言 vs 161's "未夹带修复，待裁决" — the 方案 itself makes the裁决建议； if user approves plan, that's the裁决. OK. But note §6 risk table doesn't mention R1 test-assertion change risk. Minor.
  - U2: "用户批准本计划即视为预先完成 E2 拍板" — this is a significant authorization design. 55 line 15/16: 149/151 user rulings: 字典一律 pending 不自动 confirm、首批 ≤200 条. E2 圈定 was a user stop point (README 71: "E2 圈定引用 152 E5 清单"; 方案 §2.3: "E2 圈定是用户停点"). The 方案 converts the stop point into "approve this plan = approve E2 rule" with 附录 A keyword rules. Is this 越权？ It's a pre-approval mechanism — arguably legitimate IF the user explicitly approves 附录 A. Risk: blanket approval of a plan may not constitute informed approval of specific value-domain selection; mitigations: pending-only, ≤20 类 ≤200 条， conflict flag, dry-run, 待定位清单. Also §6 gives fallback: 不批则 R2 仅 E1. Design has a safety valve. But there's a subtlety: 附录 A pre-selects categories like 科室/病区， 医生职称， 费别 — importing department/staff-title dictionaries as value domains could be large and low-value; but capped at 200. Also "离院方式" etc. overlap with already-confirmed 149 seeds — script has 不改 confirmed/冲突置位 gates. Overall design is reasonably safe; I'd say 同意 with conditions, or 疑问 on whether user realizes E2 pre-approval is bundled.

